+# Deviations from the submitted SRS, SAD and Test Plan (Member 2 work)
+
+Part-2 asks that deviations are documented and explained at the final demo. Everything below is a choice made while implementing; none changes a requirement's measurable target.
+
+| # | Document says | What was built | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | Datasets come from the Data Workspace (US-01) | Training reads the CSV through a small "locator" function (`WBMME_DATASET_LOCATOR`) | US-01 was not merged when training was built; the locator is the one place to change |
+| 2 | Login and roles from the Authentication stories | Role comes from `WBMME_ROLE_GETTER`; default uses Django staff flag and a "Data Scientist" group; a dev-only login stands in for testing | Same reason; `member2_dev/` is not part of the product |
+| 3 | SRS MLE-SR-006 gives job limits for Student and Data Scientist | Admin gets the same limit as Data Scientist (2); rate limit 60 requests per minute per user | Table has no Admin row and no rate figure; both are settings |
+| 4 | SAD: a background job | A job runs in a **separate process** started by a server thread | Needed to meet MLE-NF-006 (a failed job must not affect the server) |
+| 5 | Table 4.3-1 lists parameters and ranges | Same ranges; the random forest also fixes `n_jobs = 1` | Keeps one job from using every CPU core |
+| 6 | MLE-NF-002: 60 s on 50,000 x 20 | Features are prepared as dense arrays (sparse only for very wide tables) | The first benchmark run took 67.6 s with sparse features (limit 60 s); now 12.9 s |
+| 7 | SRS Table 4.2-1 target rules | Enforced as written (2 to 20 classes, 2 rows per class); also rejects a test share too small to stratify | scikit-learn cannot split such data |
+| 8 | Part-1 Test Plan lists test types | Added integration and system tests, a speed benchmark and a Locust load test | Covers Test Plan sections 5 and 13 and MLE-NF-002/003 |
